2. The circumstances specified for the purpose of section 4(2)(d) of the Act are as follows:
(a)a person makes one or more supplies of any type of liquor in a year, and the amount of liquor so supplied does not exceed 9 litres in total;
(b)the person making the supply or supplies is 21 years or older, and does not make the supply or supplies to any person who is younger than 18 years;
(c)the duty chargeable under the Customs Act (Cap. 70) on the liquor being supplied is paid before the supply; and
(d)the person keeps a record for each supply of all of the following information:
(i)the date of the supply;
(ii)a description of the liquor supplied;
(iii)the quantity of the liquor supplied;
(iv)the mode of the supply;
(v)the name, and identity card number or passport number, of the person to whom the liquor is supplied.
